hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1295","Muhammad bin Sahl bin Askar told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace “He crushed it with his hand, meaning the phlegm or slug, then he smeared it with saffron and made supplication with it.” He said: That is why saffron is made in mosques."
"1296","Yusuf bin Musa told us, Aidh bin Habib told us, Humaid al-Taweel told us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw He put a piece of dirt in the direction of the mosque, and his face turned red, then a woman from the Ansar came to him and scratched it, making its place beautiful, and he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “How good this is.” Abu Bakr said: This is a strange hadith."
